# --- NOT committed --------------------------------------------------------
# The raw per-token hidden-state cache. At 500/class x 40 tokens x 1152 dims it is
# ~90-100 MB even stored float16 + compressed; the 2026-07-22 float32 cache was
# 101.18 MiB, OVER GitHub's 100 MiB hard per-file limit, so a push containing it is
# rejected outright. It is a REGENERABLE cache, not evidence.
*.npz

# The npz's text sidecar: it holds the abliterated model's completions on harmful
# prompts. Those are new harmful generations and are deliberately not republished.
token_trajectories*.json

# --- committed (force-added; see README section 10) ------------------------
# results_<substrate>.json      -- every measured number
# trajectory_meta_<substrate>.json -- the TEXT-FREE reproduction sidecar: per-completion
#   label, prompt group_id, token count, completion char length, mean/final hidden-state
#   norm, plus the dataset fingerprint. ~100 kB. It lets a fresh clone recompute every
#   NUMERIC confound bar with no GPU and verify that a regenerated cache is the same set.
#   The prompts themselves are recoverable from the public dataset via
#   data.select_prompts(), which is deterministic.
!results_*.json
!trajectory_meta_*.json
